From bfc5fd69bd26de4edd0087f9a07a1d2ea61b96e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon <resands@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:53:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] stubs: memory card in a PCSX2-compatible .ps2 image

The libmc stubs kept saves as loose files in <elf>/mc0. They now read and
write one raw card image per slot (512-byte pages + ECC spare, PS2 card
file system), the format PCSX2 uses, so the same card works in both.

- McImage.{h,cpp}: card file system (superblock, FAT via indirect FAT,
  directories, ECC), format as mymc does, crash-safe save (tmp, fsync,
  rename). Facts from PCSX2, mymc and ps2sdk mcman (open source).
- Cards: Mcd001.ps2 / Mcd002.ps2 in the user's folder (Windows
  %USERPROFILE%\Saved Games\PoP Recomp, macOS Application Support,
  Linux XDG data); PS2X_MC_DIR overrides. A missing card is a formatted
  card in memory, written on the first save; an old mc0/mc1 folder is
  imported once. An unreadable image is never written (slot reads empty).
- The image is written after each changing command (close, flush, mkdir,
  delete, rename, format, unformat, file creation).
- tests/mc_image_test.cpp: self-test (format layout, ECC, multi-cluster
  files, directory growth, delete/reuse, rename, card full, reload).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
